                <pb facs="0745" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9111/653: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-29T09:00:00+03:25">August 29, 1938—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. Legation’s telegram 52 [<hi rendition="#italic">53</hi>], May 25, 11 a.m. I
                    have just learned from a source believed to be trustworthy that while Soheily
                    was Minister of Foreign Affairs he suggested to the Shah the reopening of the
                    Iranian Legation in Washington and that the Shah rejected the suggestion saying
                    that the Americans had been rude to Iran.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
